Z||000000||1FST2M6||11-29-2001||03:19 PM||||Durrell Womack (shop customer) has an 87 Silver GT 4spd. bone stock. the radio will not hold the memory once you open the car door. if you open the door with the key on and hit the horn the interior lights brighten. if you pull the key out (off obviously) and hit the horn the interior lights brighten. if the doors STAY closed and you dukes of hazzard the door the radio will keep the memory stations. (stock radio, working factory sub/slide/amp) the ONLY thing that he has done to the car was a K&N drop in. anyone have any clue. i've traced wires i've fought for hours on this thing and all i get is <B>NOTHING</B> stupid thing. I've told him to go buy a new radio speakers and amp i'd rewire the entire thing for him. but i still don't know what to do about the horn not working.. the interior lights do.. if you hook 12v directly to the horn it works.. and i checked continuity with the horn/ground/and button it SHOULD work. <B>HELP</B><P><BR>I'll be putting an Eclipse TV, PS2, 3 sets of MBquart 4" coaxial, an eclipse 35x4 and a 100x1(sub) in saturday... i'll be sure to post pics. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst2m6sig_1.gif"> <P> <A HREF="http://www.1fst2m6.com" TARGET=_blank>www.1fst2m6.com</A>  - underconstruction - but check it out anywho...||||reg||1
Z||000001||Turbo88||11-29-2001||03:26 PM||||A blown fuse caused simular problems with me. Some where there is a loss of connectivity that is causing the radio to loose memory. All I would say is check the fuses with an ohm meter (some times they don't look blown but they are <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">). Kinda obvious but ya never know! Good Luck||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||11-29-2001||03:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Turbo88:<BR><B>A blown fuse caused simular problems with me. Some where there is a loss of connectivity that is causing the radio to loose memory. ... </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ditto. Had the same problem with my old 87 GT. Replaced the blown fuse and the problem went away. By the way, I found the solution to my problem by asking here! Just like you. Kinda neat.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P><B>JUST ADDED: </B>1988 GT w/ T-Tops, 5-Speed, and Performance Sound.||||reg||1
Z||000003||kempo||11-29-2001||03:52 PM||||I'm with them.  Check ALL fuses.  I had so many electrical problems, even worse than what you are describing, 1fst2m6.  Due to the cigarette lighter, my floor courtesy lights would come on, ignition on and running or not, and stay on.  With the doors open, the courtesy overhead and map lights would not light.  Close the door, try it, and the floor lights would go out.  Turn on both map lights and they would both go out and the floor lights would glow extremely bright.  Hit the lock or unlock button with both doors closed and the rear decklid release would go off and pop the hood.  All the while my radio was blowing fuses causing parking light / insturment guage lighting / headlight motors to stop working, due to a faulty unit.  <P>Electrical problems are the worst, most time consuming and annoying problems.  Bless your soul and best of luck!<BR>ALSO- make sure that the right size fuses are inserted into the correct socket, cause of many problems to come.||||reg||3
